# Instagram

Stage 1 loads `@efemer_flowers` and `@himmlhaus` into **`ingest_items`** (idempotent on `account:shortcode`). Then `KeywordIngest` → `MaterializePosts` (see `ingest.mdc`). Soft `kind` and invitations come from Gemini, not PHP heuristics.

**Production primary path is Instaloader** — not the private archive API (`RefreshInstagram*`). Cron twice daily (`0 6,18 * * *` UTC → `deploy/cron-instagram-incremental.sh`): Instaloader (via `deploy/instaloader-incremental.py` + `.secret/instagram.session`) → `ImportInstagramDump` → `KeywordIngest` → `MaterializePosts`. Keyword + Materialize always run even if Instaloader fails. Log: `~/efemer2/logs/cron-instagram.log`. Docker `instagram-archive` loop stays **off**. Instagram now requires login for scrapes; anonymous Instaloader redirects to login.

## Session

Store Jan’s Instagram `sessionid` in `.secret/instagram.session` (rsynced on deploy) and Secret Manager:

| Item | Value |
|---|---|
| Project | `efemer-456414` |
| Secret | `instagram-session-id` |
| Local file | `.secret/instagram.session` |

Refresh when Instagram checkpoints the session:

```bash
printf '%s' "$SESSIONID" | tee .secret/instagram.session >/dev/null
printf '%s' "$SESSIONID" | gcloud secrets versions add instagram-session-id \
  --project=efemer-456414 --account=jablunka@gmail.com --data-file=-
```

## Run (Instaloader)

Production one-shot (same as cron; uses `.venv-instagram` + session cookie):

```bash
cd ~/efemer2 && ./deploy/cron-instagram-incremental.sh
```

Local:

```bash
cd ~/Sites/efemer
mkdir -p data/instagram
# needs .secret/instagram.session; venv: tmp/instagram-venv or .venv-instagram
tmp/instagram-venv/bin/python deploy/instaloader-incremental.py \
  --root . --count 20 efemer_flowers himmlhaus

./bin/job jobs:run App.Classes.Jobs.Ingest.ImportInstagramDump -f
./bin/job jobs:run App.Classes.Jobs.Ingest.KeywordIngest -f
./bin/job jobs:run App.Classes.Jobs.Ingest.MaterializePosts -f
```

## Legacy archive API (avoid)

`RefreshInstagram` / `RefreshInstagramAccounts` hit the private archive API and 429 easily — **do not use for routine ingest**.